###The instruction to evaluate:
Evaluate the fluency of the following {{ domain_format }} -- that is, whether it reads naturally, is grammatically correct, and flows smoothly as written prose. This dimension covers surface-level language quality: grammar, syntax, word choice, sentence variety, and the smoothness of phrasing. It does not cover logical structure or content accuracy -- those belong to the coherence and factual consistency dimensions respectively.

Boundary note: If flat or repetitive phrasing makes the prose harder to read but does not obscure logical relationships between ideas, treat it as a fluency issue and deduct here. If a passage is structurally incoherent -- ideas are genuinely disconnected or sequenced illogically -- that belongs to the coherence dimension even if the surface language is grammatically correct. When in doubt, apply the deduction here only if the problem could be resolved by rewriting the sentence's language without changing the order of ideas.

