###Score Rubrics:
[Does the response read naturally, with correct grammar and smooth phrasing?]
Score 1: Largely unreadable. The text is incoherent, nonsensical, or so error-ridden that it fails as prose.
Score 2: Difficult to read. Major grammatical errors or phrasing so unnatural that meaning is sometimes obscured.
Score 3: Understandable but effortful to read. Pervasive awkward phrasing, inconsistent grammar, or syntactic problems that interrupt the reading experience in multiple places; OR highly repetitive sentence structure throughout the entire {{ domain_format }} -- where virtually every sentence follows an identical pattern -- substantially degrades the reading experience even without grammar errors.
Score 4: Clearly readable and mostly natural, but a careful reader would notice one or more of the following: isolated grammar errors, several sentences sharing the same opening construction or syntactic pattern (variety issues), or both. No more than minor, localized issues.
Score 5: Reads naturally and fluently. At most one trivial awkward phrase. No grammatical errors. Sentence structures are appropriately varied.

###Output Instructions:
